In the image above is a model of the Pitts S-3 Special Aircraft. It has the characteristics of the original Pitts S-2 (in fact of three and half model in 1/32), but has a smaller wing and a streamlined fuselage. I wanted to build the S-3 because of too many different models of this plane of the same company. I think that I managed to reproduce the real appearance of aircraft, but I just don’t know if it works as the real plane. It was only a model and I am sorry because it falls to the ground.
In the original the S-2 was used with the rocket R943 and was flown from an altitude of more than 6000 feet to a vertical speed of 450 m/s. It does not look like a rocket plane, but is a rocket plane of the very first model of the company Pitts and still I will build a model of this plane in 1:144

